Feature: Customer dropdown # features/00_home_page.feature:1
  As a user opening the home page
  I want to see a customer dropdown
  So that I can select a customer
  Scenario: Default option shows "Select Customer"          # features/00_home_page.feature:6
    Given the app is running                                # steps/home_steps.py:81
    When I open the home page                               # steps/home_steps.py:91
    Then the customer dropdown default is "Select Customer" # steps/home_steps.py:97

  Scenario: Customer dropdown is rendered and functional    # features/00_home_page.feature:10
    Given I am on the home page                             # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I click the customer dropdown                      # steps/home_steps.py:144
    Then the dropdown should be visible and contain options # steps/home_steps.py:152

  @api
  Scenario: Customer dropdown is populated from API and selection persists  # features/00_home_page.feature:16
    Given I am on the home page                                             # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I wait for the customer dropdown to be populated from the API      # steps/home_steps.py:109
    And I select the first available customer                               # steps/home_steps.py:114
    Then the selected customer remains selected in the dropdown             # steps/home_steps.py:136

Feature: Primary navigation from Home # features/01_navigation.feature:1
  As a user
  I want to move between core pages from the Home page
  So that I can complete key flows
  Background:   # features/01_navigation.feature:6

  Scenario: Navigate from Home to Purchase Rings to Manage Orders to About Us  # features/01_navigation.feature:10
    Given the app is running                                                   # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I open the home page                                                   # steps/navigation_steps.py:65
    When I navigate to "Purchase Rings"                                        # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "Purchase Rings" page                              # steps/navigation_steps.py:99
    When I navigate to "Manage Orders"                                         # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "Manage Orders" page                               # steps/navigation_steps.py:99
    When I navigate to "About Us"                                              # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "About Us" page                                    # steps/navigation_steps.py:99

  Scenario: Cart nav link navigates to the cart page  # features/01_navigation.feature:20
    Given the app is running                          # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I open the home page                          # steps/navigation_steps.py:65
    When I navigate to "Cart"                         # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "Cart" page               # steps/navigation_steps.py:99

  Scenario: Logo click navigates back to the home page  # features/01_navigation.feature:24
    Given the app is running                            # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I open the home page                            # steps/navigation_steps.py:65
    Given I navigate to "Purchase Rings"                # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    When I click the site logo                          # steps/navigation_steps.py:107
    Then I should be on the "Home" page                 # steps/navigation_steps.py:99

  Scenario: Cart badge shows the number of items in the cart  # features/01_navigation.feature:29
    Given the app is running                                  # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I open the home page                                  # steps/navigation_steps.py:65
    Given I navigate to "Purchase Rings"                      # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    And the purchase rings page is ready                      # steps/navigation_steps.py:114
    When I add the first ring to the cart                     # steps/navigation_steps.py:122
    Then the cart badge should show 1                         # steps/navigation_steps.py:132

Feature: Shopping Cart # features/02_cart.feature:1
  As a user with items in my cart
  I want to manage my cart and checkout
  So that I can complete my purchase
  Background:   # features/02_cart.feature:6

  Scenario: Cart page shows the Shopping Cart heading  # features/02_cart.feature:10
    Given the app is running                           # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                          # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I navigate to "Cart"                          # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then the cart page heading should be visible       # steps/cart.steps.py:120

  Scenario: Empty cart shows correct message      # features/02_cart.feature:14
    Given the app is running                      # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                     # steps/home_steps.py:85
    Given I ensure the cart is empty              # steps/cart.steps.py:20
    Then the empty cart message should be visible # steps/cart.steps.py:131

  Scenario: Continue Shopping link from empty cart navigates to Purchase Rings  # features/02_cart.feature:18
    Given the app is running                                                    # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                                                   # steps/home_steps.py:85
    Given I ensure the cart is empty                                            # steps/cart.steps.py:20
    When I click the empty cart Continue Shopping link                          # steps/cart.steps.py:35
    Then I should be on the "Purchase Rings" page                               # steps/navigation_steps.py:99

  Scenario: Cart displays items after a ring is added  # features/02_cart.feature:23
    Given the app is running                           # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                          # steps/home_steps.py:85
    Given I navigate to "Purchase Rings"               # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    And the purchase rings page is ready               # steps/navigation_steps.py:114
    When I add the first ring to the cart              # steps/navigation_steps.py:122
    And I navigate to "Cart"                           # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then the cart should contain at least 1 item       # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:189

  Scenario: Order summary section is visible in a populated cart  # features/02_cart.feature:30
    Given the app is running                                      # steps/home_steps.py:81
